        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275-a7">

                <pb facs="0785" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v27/pg747"/>

                <head>Annex 4</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#bold">Letter From Foreign Secretary Lloyd to
                        Secretary of State Dulles<anchor n="16" xml:id="d275-f1"/></hi></p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#italic">Bermuda, March 23, 1957.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Foster</hi>: Thank you for your letter of
                    23rd March, 1957, enclosing a memorandum of conversation regarding intermediate
                    range ballistic missiles, which was one of the topics which the Prime Minister
                    and I discussed yesterday afternoon with the President, Deputy Secretary
                    Robertson, Secretary Quarles, Admiral Strauss and yourself.</p>
                <p>I am glad to confirm that this memorandum represents the understanding of the
                    United Kingdom side in this matter.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Selwyn Lloyd</hi><anchor n="17"
                            xml:id="d275-f2"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
